Tzamouranis, Winnie Lambert, Mark Leeds, Nick Ellis and Professor Brian D. 
Ripley):

 

On Wed, 31 Mar 2004 
Agin.Patrick at hydro.qc.ca wrote: 

> Hi, 
> I'm using S-Plus with 
calls to C functions. It works very well but I'm 
> 
wondering if there is mean to enter the C debugger while debugging the 

> calls to C? I'm using Microsoft Visual C++ 7.0 and 
S-Plus 4.5 on 
> Windows XP. Thank 
you, 
 

The 
required steps are the following :

1- 
create your DLL with these parameters set for debugging (under the 
property pages/configuration properties)

  configuration set to Debug and platform to 
Win32

  under 
  Action, set command to the path of the S-Plus executable (ex: c:\Program 
  Files\splus45\cmd\splus.exe)

  under 
  Action, set command arguments to S_PROJ={your current project chapter} (ex: 
  S_PROJ="c:\my_splus_project" or S_PROJ=. for the current 
  directory)

2- set 
some breakpoints and start debugging (make sure that you have not an S-Plus 
session already opened). In my case, a window appears saying: 
"SPLUS.EXE does not contain debugging information. (Exports loaded.) 
Click OK to debug anyway". Click OK. It starts an S-Plus 
session.

3- 
Switch to S-Plus and call your program. When executing the .C call, it should 
break in the VC debugger.

 

Thank 
you to all for your help,

Patrick 

