From zaslavsk at hcp.med.harvard.edu  Sun Apr  4 19:24:28 2004
From: zaslavsk at hcp.med.harvard.edu (Alan Zaslavsky)
Date: Sun, 04 Apr 2004 15:24:28 -0400
Subject: Re: Multiple R-Squared
In-Reply-To: <BAY16-DAV48GQhGponi0000f9ff@hotmail.com>
References: <BAY16-DAV48GQhGponi0000f9ff@hotmail.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.05.10404041519140.8754-100000@elixir.hcp.med.harvard.edu>

The R-square is calculated based on variance explained relative to a null
model.  For a model with an intercept the null model includes an intercept
(constant model), but for a model without an intercept the null model has
not intercept (constant=0 model).  Thus with fairly similar residual
variances, the R-square could be quite different (since the mean squared
error of the no-intercept null model could be much larger if the mean is
large).

