From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Sun Apr  4 19:37:31 2004
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Sun, 04 Apr 2004 20:37:31 +0100
Subject: Re: Multiple R-Squared
In-Reply-To: <BAY16-DAV48GQhGponi0000f9ff@hotmail.com>
References: <BAY16-DAV48GQhGponi0000f9ff@hotmail.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44.0404042008320.26080-100000@gannet.stats>

On Sun, 4 Apr 2004, Chushu Gu wrote:

> I got confused with multiple R-Square, Here are the analysis I did.
> After I force the linear regression line pass the origin, the multiple
> R-square increase from 0.78 to 0.98. Anyone wo know how they define
> multiple R-Square please help.

        R^2 = 1- residual sum of squares / RSS for minimal model

The minimal model is the fitted model with all the terms removed, so it 
has an intercept if and only if the fitted model does.

In words, the fit is compared to that of a constant prediction of the
mean if there is an intercept, and to the constant prediction of zero
otherwise.

