I interpreted Burnham and Anderson's formula as:

Loglik = (-n / 2) * LN(RSE^2 * df / n) - (n / 2) * LN(2*PI()) - (n / 2)

With

RSE = residual standard error (in output)

df = degrees of freedom on the RSE

n = sample size

and for linear models came to the same loglik and AIC that SPlus gave me

